; step_limit_at_the_counter_ceiling: a run under a step limit of 2^64 - 1.
;
; The step counter is a u64, and the largest limit a host can set is the
; counter's own ceiling -- the limit an unbounded budget stands for
; (spec/xqvm/METERING.md, The Step Counter). Under it a run is metered
; exactly as under any other limit: every instruction pays BASE_STEPS and
; SETLINE pays COEFF_WRITE_STEPS on top, and the count it reports is the
; count it spent. No program can carry the counter past 2^64 - 1 in a test's
; lifetime, so the refusal at the ceiling is pinned by crate tests on both
; VMs rather than here.

PUSH 2
BQMX r0
PUSH 0
PUSH 3
SETLINE r0
PUSH 0
GETLINE r0
HALT
